   117	/* The caml_gc_phase global is only ever updated at the end of the STW
   118	   section, by the last domain leaving a barrier. This means that no
   119	   synchronization is required on most accesses.
   120	
   121	   We know of two situations in the runtime that could run in parallel
   122	   with a phase update, and cannot safely access the gc phase:
   123	
   124	   - The caml_domain_terminate logic runs after the thread has un-registered
   125	     itself as a STW participant, so it may race with a STW section.
   126	
   127	   - Opportunistic collections may happen while a domain is waiting on
   128	     a STW barrier, so it might race with the code running inside
   129	     another in-STW barrier. (It is possible that a deeper analysis of
   130	     the current runtime code would in fact rule out such a race, but
   131	     it is simpler to avoid phase accesses during opportunistic
   132	     collections.)
   133	 */
